ting correlate on Models 1, 2, 3","toolSummary":"Test all models root causes"}}]}
{"step_index":1040,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:18:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-20T00:48:57+05:30\nTool is running as a background task with task id: f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/task-1040\nTask Description: python -c \"\nfrom modules.production_analyzer import load_dataset, analyze\nfrom modules.root_cause import correlate\n\nfor m_num in [1, 2, 3]:\n    p = 'D:/acceleration/Model_' + str(m_num) + '.csv'\n    df, _ = load_dataset(p)\n    a = analyze(df)\n    cards = correlate(a, {'by_type': {'crack': 5, 'scratch': 3}})\n    print('=== Model ' + str(m_num) + ': ' + str(len(cards)) + ' evidence cards ===')\n    for c in cards:\n        print('  [' + c['confidence'] + '] ' + c['cause'])\n        print('      Evidence: ' + c['evidence'])\n\"\n\nTask logs are available at: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/.system_generated/tasks/task-1040.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
