{"step_index":1075,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:21:17Z","content":"### Why Model 2 and Model 3 Previously Showed No Root Cause:\n\n1. **Model 3 (13 Stations: `Blanking`, `Press1-4`, `Cell1-4`, `Paint1-2`, `Quality`, `Forklift`)**:\n   - The original static rules only checked hardcoded names: `'Drilling Util'`, `'Milling Util'`, and `'Assembly Util'`.\n   - In **Model 3**, the primary constraint is **`Cell1`** (operating at a critical **86.7% capacity utilization**), along with high loads at **`Blanking` (85.3%)** and **`Cell4` (81.4%)**. Because the rule engine didn't dynamically map non-standard station names, it bypassed these overloads.\n\n2. **Model 2 (`Drilling`, `Milling`, `Assembly`)**:\n   - The original hardcoded rule required `> 85%` utilization to trigger an alert.\n   - In **Model 2**, the line operates at a moderate pace where the primary bottleneck is **`Assembly` at 68.4% utilization** and **`Drilling` at 52.1%**. Because 68.4% was below the static 85% threshold, no rule fired.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Upgraded & Fixed in the Root Cause Engine:\n\nWe upgraded [`modules/root_cause.py`](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/root_cause.py) with a **Dynamic Theory of Constraints (TOC) Causal Framework**:\n\n- **Dynamic Station Mapping**: Automatically detects any station type across arbitrary simulation topologies (Stamping, Presses, Cells, Machining, Coating, Assembly, Quality buffers) and correlates its specific physical failure mechanisms to defect manifestations (e.g., cell fixture stress &rarr; cracks/scratches; stamping impact &rarr; cracks/holes; coating &rarr; rust).\n- **Multi-Tiered Utilization Thresholds**:\n  - **Critical Overload (&ge;80%)**: Emits **HIGH** confidence alert for major constraint bottlenecks (e.g., `Cell1` and `Blanking` in Model 3).\n  - **Moderate Line Constraint (60%–80%)**: Emits **MEDIUM** confidence advisory for line pacing and component fitment friction (e.g., `Assembly` in Model 2).\n  - **Active Workload (50%–60%)**: Emits **LOW** confidence baseline wear diagnostics (e.g., `Drilling` in Model 2).\n- **Queue Backlog & Dwell Latency Diagnostics**: Detects upstream buffer accumulation (&gt;6 min queue delays) that cause surface oxidation and handling damage.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Across All Models:\n\n| Model | Generated Evidence Cards | Key Diagnostic Findings |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Model 1** | **5 Evidence Cards** | Drilling queue micro-cracks (`31.2 min`), Assembly extreme delay (`97.1 min`), Assembly constraint (`77.6%`). |\n| **Model 2** | **2 Evidence Cards** | Assembly primary constraint (`68.4%` util), Drilling baseline workload (`52.1%` util). |\n| **Model 3** | **13 Evidence Cards** | `Cell1` Critical TOC Bottleneck (`86.7%`), `Blanking` overload (`85.3%`), `Cell4` overload (`81.4%`), Press/Quality queue buffers. |"}
